  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The political environment in Kenya has intensified following a recent dispute at an Independent Electoral and Boundaries Commission (IEBC) meeting. Opposition members exited the session after representatives from the ruling coalition were invited to speak, prompting criticism from government officials who argued the walkout prevented constructive dialogue regarding electoral concerns. Subsequently, public discourse has focused on the cohesion of the opposition alliance. While some observers speculated about the emergence of competing factions or a 'third force' within the opposition, leaders such as Fred Matiang’i and Ndindi Nyoro have explicitly dismissed these claims. They maintained that the opposition is working toward a singular, unified approach to challenge President William Ruto in the upcoming 2027 general elections. Meanwhile, members of the ruling United Democratic Alliance have continued to urge their rivals to engage respectfully with independent national institutions.",
